# MVVM-C (XQ Finance)

Follow `docs/mvvm-c.md`. This rule is opt-in via globs so it does not fight
`xq-squad.mdc` (`alwaysApply: true`).

## Do

- Put feature `navigationDestination` and `.sheet(item:)` only in `*CoordinatorView.swift`.
- Use `NavigationLink(value:)` with coordinator-owned route enums (**D6**).
- Keep path/sheet mutations in `FitnessTabCoordinator` / `FinanceTabCoordinator`.
- Keep packages SwiftUI-free; construct persistence in bootstrap/DI, not Views.
- Treat accessibility IDs in `FinanceAccessibility` / `FitnessAccessibility` /
  `SuperAppAccessibility` as **frozen** unless the task flags an ID change.
- Prefer pure refactors: live UX stays unchanged unless the task names a UX change.

## Do not

- Use `NavigationLink(destination:)`.
- Call `store.send` / `importSnapshot` or reference `ProductionFinancePersistence` /
  `FileManager.default` / `PortfolioStore` inside `*View.swift`.
- Introduce `@EnvironmentObject` / `@StateObject` / `ObservableObject` for app
  feature stores/coordinators/VMs.
- Edit the managed `AGENTS.md` block between `XQ_SQUAD_MANAGED_*` markers.

Nested `NavigationStack` inside editor/sheet chrome is allowed. `#Preview` code is
ignored by `scripts/check-architecture.sh`.
